WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.130
The Federation's Torrington Base
has been reduced to a pile of rubble.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.590
Uraki's heart is shaken
by the experience...

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.120
...of losing teammates in
battle for the first time.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:20.430
New pilots have been posted to
the assault carrier <i>Albion...</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.440
...but a fierce dislike
has formed between...

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.810
...Uraki and veteran pilot Monsha.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.110
As Uraki finally won the right to
sit in the pilot's seat of Unit 1...

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.050
...the order came
to recover Unit 2.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.920
With various feelings
in her crew's hearts...

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.750
...the <i>Albion</i> sets
off into battle.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:01:02.330
Mobile Suit Gundam 0083

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:08.530
shourisha nado inai tatakai ni tsukare hate
There's no winner of this fight as I collapse, now exhausted.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.500
hoshizora o miageru
I look up to the stars above...

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.170
naku koto mo kanawanai
...and don't even have the strength to cry.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:19.540
I don't need kinou nado iranai
I don't need, don't need yesterday anymore.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.820
I don't need kuchi hateta yume mo
I don't need dreams that have crumbled away.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.050
I got a burning heart!

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.050
mune o tsuranuku suriru wo
I just wanna keep on running!

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:37.890
tada oi kakete hashiri tsuzuketai
Just chasing the thrill that's shooting through my heart!

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.560
kotoba ni dekinai omoi ga
Feelings that you just can't describe with words...

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:50.450
kogoeta kokoro sae atsuku saseru
...are enough to ignite even a frozen heart!

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.110
I got a burning love!

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:57.180
aoku kagayaku honoo de
Burning with shining blue fire.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.900
kono hoshizora o ooi tsukusu toki made
Fire that'll spread until it covers all the stars in the sky.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:06.260
I got a burning heart!

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.390
ai wa kodoku na tatakai
Love is such a lonely battle.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:15.200
kono sekai made moyashi tsukusu no ka
But is it one that will consume the world in flames?

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.070
ATTACK AND RETREAT
ON THE BURNING SAND

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.870
The enemy?! Ivan,
prep for evasive maneuvers!

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.670
No, sir. It's not the enemy.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.780
What?

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:19.280
It's the port side mobile
suit deck. Well, it's...

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.380
Simone, you're not saying...

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.720
'Fraid I am, Lieutenant.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.180
Would you cut it out?!

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.450
Not a bad punch, Miss Amazon.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.060
But we can't just let you
beat up our pal for kicks.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.760
Oh, spare me!

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.070
Do your duties include looking
for womens' asses to pinch?!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.800
Back off!

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.400
Just whose fault is it
we were dragged out...

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.410
...into the middle of nowhere
for this African safari?

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.450
- Secure the ego, fly boy!
- Yeah! Yeah!

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.080
Don't be jealous, sister.
I'll have a talk with Monsha.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.150
I'll make sure he pinches
your ass, too, next time.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.430
<i>Now you did it, you sag!</i>

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:08.950
<i>The word's HAG, moron! A real man</i>
<i>is a gentleman, like the captain!</i>

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.430
<i>Oh? Didn't know you went</i>
<i>in for older men.</i>

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:12.960
<i>That... That's ridiculous!</i>

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.470
<i>Nina, honey!</i>

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.030
<i>You want more, you ass?!</i>

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:19.700
Those idiots! How long are they
gonna play around like kids?!

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.950
Mr. Burning!

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:27.040
This ship and its crew haven't
had time to be properly broken in.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.750
These little disturbances
aren't helping matters.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.050
Aye, sir.
I'm sorry about this.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.150
I'll discipline the
pilots immediately!

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.360
Don't they understand <i>I</i> want
to cut loose as much as they do?!

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.060
Those idiots!

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.070
Oh, I am sick and tired
of those pilots!

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.200
They act like they're
the stars of the show!

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:52.570
Watch that mouth, Chief.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.470
Sorry, sir!

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.950
We haven't picked up Gato's
trail in this past week.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.150
Everyone's sick to death of
looking at the African scenery.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.750
Captain, we've got
<i>another</i> message from Jaburo.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.920
That's the third one today...

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.550
It's not like we
can ignore them!

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.260
Um...

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:16.500
Sorry. Patch it through.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.100
<i>Searching for the</i>
<i>stolen Gundam Unit 2...</i>

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.800
<i>...the</i> Albion <i>now</i>
<i>wanders across Africa.</i>

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.770
<i>Traces of Minovsky particles and</i>
<i>the heat shimmers of the savanna...</i>

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:34.410
<i>...conceal Unit 2 and seem</i>
<i>to laugh at our frustration.</i>

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:38.950
<i>The Earth's environment has</i>
<i>too wide a range of expressions.</i>

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.420
<i>If something</i>
<i>doesn't happen soon...</i>

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.120
<i>...I'll probably end up as</i>
<i>on edge as everyone else is.</i>

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.790
<i>I know how frustrated</i>
<i>they feel, but...</i>

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.800
Miss Purpleton. Nina Purpleton!

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:55.040
Do you agree with
what he just said?

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:56.770
What? What who just said?

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:59.780
<i>We've already accepted delivery</i>
<i>of Unit 2 from Anaheim!</i>

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:03.410
<i>If recovering it is too much</i>
<i>trouble, I say just destroy it!</i>

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.940
<i>And to hell with what that</i>
<i>Lunarian on board with you thinks!</i>

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:08.080
What did you say?!

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.990
We'll do our best. I'll increase
patrols at once. Over and out!

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.160
<i>W- Wait!</i>

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:21.090
Miss Purpleton, I hope you
can forgive his rudeness.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:25.100
No, it's all right.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:27.330
The brass don't have a clue!

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:31.400
And why are we the only
ones running the search?!

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:36.280
Lt. Harida, there are a great
many ships combing this continent.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:37.750
It's not just us.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:40.940
All of them are ships
attached to Admiral Kowen.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.390
The guys at Jaburo are so scared of
Unit 2 firing the nuke at them...

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.620
...they're racing around
like bees in a hive!

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:51.390
All of you! This ship
is carrying out an operation!

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.090
Now stop this behavior now!

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:09.040
Kilimanjaro area is clear.
Requesting landing clearance.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:13.040
<i>Roger. Readying landing bay.</i>
<i>Please stand by.</i>

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.780
Roger.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.450
What's with this hand?!
You wanna bankrupt me?!

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:27.130
Quit complaining. Didn't you
start this game to kill some time?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.100
You guys sure don't
act like friends!

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.770
<i>Port side deck, prepare</i>
<i>to receive core fighter.</i>

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:36.770
<i>All personnel, to your stations.</i>

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.370
Looks like Uraki's back.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.430
Probably empty-handed, too.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.940
Uraki, huh? All right!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.420
Let's change my luck
with one last bet.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.370
Half a month's pay that
Uraki can't do it.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:17.380
And I'll bet what you
owe me that he can.

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:18.910
Count me out.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.450
Whatever you want, Ensign.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:38.760
- I win! Now we're even!
- Heh, clumsy kid.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.030
Hold it! You did this, right!
What were you thinking?!

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.770
You, again? We were just
givin' Uraki a little training.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:50.000
This is our only
spare core fighter!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.710
What happens if it gets
knocked out of commission?!

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.910
Oh, really?! You mean the
Academy golden boy can't land...

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:57.940
...without someone
holding his hand?!

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:04.850
Lieutenant! It's been decided that
Ensign Uraki will pilot Unit 1!

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.730
Nina! I just had a little
too much to drink that time.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.430
If I took him on now,
I wouldn't screw up like that.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.900
I hate people
with no self control!

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:19.200
H- Hate?!
Nina, don't say that!

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.440
Let's go, Ensign Uraki.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.330
Hey! Running away, Uraki?!
Wait! I want a rematch!

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.960
God dammit!

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.370
Lieutenant, you'll just
piss her off even more.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:48.000
I know! I know!
Just keep your yap shut!

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:50.370
Shit, I hate being on standby!

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:52.240
Where the hell are
those Zeeks hiding?!

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.670
S- Sorry, sir!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.770
Dammit!
What's the big hurry?!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.040
B- Biological emergency, sir!

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:06.040
Calm down, it won't kill you!
And stay on the left side!

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:11.650
For God's sake, I warned you.
Aw, to hell with it...

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:12.980
Oh, well...

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.220
I'm kinda in a hurry.
Sorry! Sorry! Sorry!

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.330
Get going.
I know how you feel...

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.770
Thanks!

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.680
To the rebirth of Zeon.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:46.280
To the success of
Operation Stardust.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.320
Delicious.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.700
The last bottle I've been keeping.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.330
If I'm going to drink with
the hero of my men...

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.340
...champagne is only
appropriate, Commander.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.340
You're an inspiration
to all soldiers, sir.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:07.000
You've done well to maintain this
underground base for 3 years.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.010
I've lost a lot of good men.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:13.350
We only have 10 operational
mobile suits left.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:16.880
Since we set up this base in
an abandoned diamond mine...

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:20.880
...it really wasn't
that difficult to build.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.390
Well, at the very least...

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.990
...it'll allow me to get the
stolen Gundam out to space.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.400
Do whatever you
have to, Commander.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:34.740
At least maintaining that last
HLV turned out to be worth it.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.710
Sir, you're doing so much for me,
and yet I can't tell you why...

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:42.710
That's part of any plan.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:46.980
All we have to do is wait till
the launch time and use the HLV...

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:50.210
...to get you to the rendezvous
point with the recovery ship.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:53.690
And do this while hiding our
presence from the enemy.

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:54.950
Sir...

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.690
All for the birth of a new Zeon.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:10.640
There he is!

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:15.430
<i>To all guards!</i>
<i>Anaheim staff member Orville...</i>

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:17.880
...has run to the vicinity
of the port side launch deck!

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.210
So, he was a Zeon spy, huh?

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:25.550
Captain! The core fighter
launch hatch is opening!

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.220
St- Stop!

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:49.400
Okay, we've let him get away.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.540
Scott, don't lose him!

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:52.870
Aye, sir!

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.680
Captain, I'm sorry about this.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.520
That the spy was from Anaheim...

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.860
You've nothing to be
sorry about, Miss Purpleton.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:07.490
And thanks to this, we'll be
able to find the enemy base.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.230
Yes, sir.

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:18.030
Blau Engel to Kimbareid!
Blau Engel to Kimbareid!

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.340
Please respond!
I've escaped from the <i>Albion.</i>

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:32.480
She's an old HLV, but she'll
get you into orbit all right.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:35.720
Excellent! There's no way
I can thank you for this, sir.

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:42.830
Launching this in one hour may
be this base's greatest triumph.

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:43.460
Yes, sir.

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.470
Excuse me, sir.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:46.520
What is it?

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:50.340
A message from Blau Engel.
He's escaped from the enemy ship.

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:51.810
Orville, from Anaheim?!

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.500
Oh, no! Don't answer him!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:56.440
If we do, we could reveal the
base's position to the enemy!

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:57.840
Yes, sir!

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:02.840
Hold it. Even if we don't respond,
he might lead them to us.

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:04.480
This is turning bad.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:11.860
Sir, just what we wanted!
Orville's trying to contact the Zeon!

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.260
Lieutenant Burning, do you
hear me? Send them out!

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:18.520
Roger! Time to say
goodbye to those binoculars!

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:23.100
Monsha, you're A team's leader!

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:24.870
Roger!

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:30.480
B team is Bate and Adel!
You'll stand by here!

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.500
Huh? What?

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.810
Lieutenant, are you saying?!

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:37.120
<i>Monsha, you're taking Uraki</i>
<i>and Keith with you!</i>

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:39.120
We're not going sightseeing!

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.420
<i>That's an order!</i>

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.820
Captain, can he make an
assignment like that?!

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:45.560
Lt. Burning has authority over
all mobile suit operations.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.320
I don't need a couple
of bed wetting babies!

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.860
Bed wetting babies?!

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:56.000
We'll follow you with
diapers ready, Lieutenant Monsha.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.200
Hah! Is that
supposed to be a joke?

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:04.880
Oh! Nina, darling!
Now, where's that sub-camera?

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.850
<i>Nina, watch your feet!</i>

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.050
What's <i>with</i> you?!

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:16.680
Send 'em out!

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:31.400
Shit! Everything looks
the same around here!

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:40.550
Thank God! They sent
a greeting party!

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.150
What are you doing?! Stop it!

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:01.100
Where are you, space men?!
I'll show you a good time!

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.500
<i>Lieutenant, they prefer</i>
<i>to be called Spacenoids.</i>

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.440
<i>Well, pardon my ignorance!</i>

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:08.770
Lieutenant, do you always
command like this?

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:12.440
Hm? Uraki, I'm a
very stubborn SOB!

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:15.610
Don't get cocky just 'cuz
you beat me once!

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:17.410
Yes, sir.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.510
Lieutenant! At 1:30!

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:24.360
All right! This is what
I've been waiting for!

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:25.990
Let 'em have it, you two!

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:29.060
<i>L- Lieutenant! We can't</i>
<i>hit them like this!</i>

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:34.090
Ensign Uraki, that was an order.
You got that, kid?

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:35.870
Loud and clear.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:43.980
B- Beam cannons!

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:49.850
Wait! What about me?!

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:58.520
There, you see? They're leading
us right to the enemy base!

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:24.010
Sir, we've finished
fitting the boosters.

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:28.350
Good. If we're lucky, we can
take out that enemy ship.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:32.090
At the very least, we'll buy
time till we launch the HLV.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.530
Good luck, sir.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.490
- Lieutenant Val.
- Sir!

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:40.490
After I launch, you'll be
in command of this base.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:43.010
Yes, sir. What about it?

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.440
After the HLV is successfully
launched, you will surrender.

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.500
What?! But, sir...

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:51.450
If we lose our mobile
suits in this battle...

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.450
...this base will no
longer serve any purpose.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.140
We'll still fight, sir!

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.980
You men have all fought well
over these past 3 years.

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:03.460
Our will shall live on
in Operation Stardust.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.430
You mean...
With Commander Gato, sir?

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:06.830
Do what I asked.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.520
Sir!

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:19.970
All units, we're hitting the enemy
ship. Let nothing distract you!

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:38.020
You're not getting away, Spacenoids!
Not after all that waiting!

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:39.790
I'm picking up something!
To the left!

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:40.820
<i>What?!</i>

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:43.360
Shit! Reinforcements?!

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.970
That idiot!
He ran into an ambush?!

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:52.470
Aye, sir. Two Doms.

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:56.100
Unfortunately, it seems the enemy
didn't let Orville get to them.

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:59.140
Yes, sir. They led
Monsha and the others off...

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:02.520
...so we wouldn't be
able to find the base.

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.450
Send out Bate and Adel's units.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:07.320
If they're that desperate
for us not to find them...

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.190
...wouldn't that indicate
they have Gundam Unit 2?

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:13.830
The enemy base is in the direction
Orville was originally flying.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.130
<i>WHAT?! They tricked us?</i>

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.830
<i>The real base is in an</i>
<i>abandoned diamond mine?!</i>

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.830
What do you mean?!

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:25.640
Lieutenant Monsha, this was
too good to be true, wasn't it?

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:27.440
We have to rendezvous
with Lieutenant Bate!

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.310
<i>Don't be such a know-it-all!</i>

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:31.910
<i>Additional: Lieutenant Burning's</i>
<i>royally pissed at you.</i>

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:36.420
- Pull back!
- <i>B- But how?!</i>

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:39.480
<i>Even if we follow this river bed,</i>
<i>we can't get to the</i> Albion!

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.890
<i>I don't care!</i>

00:20:56.840 --> 00:21:00.470
Captain, we've completed our
turn towards the enemy base.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:03.450
All right!
All hands, battle stations!

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:05.340
We're taking the
<i>Albion</i> straight in!

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:07.040
But Captain, that's!

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:11.380
We've no choice! That feint was
clearly designed to buy time.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:14.010
They're planning to
make their move soon.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:17.150
You mean transport
Gundam Unit 2 out of here?!

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:19.890
Wh- What was?!

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:32.700
Just two mobile suits guarding it.

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:35.510
Luck's on our side. Let's go!

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:57.000
And they say the guys who stay
behind are the lucky ones!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.060
Shit! What's keeping
Monsha and Uraki?!

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:17.710
They're getting ready. They've
got the dust raised everywhere!

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:21.420
Uraki! We have no choice!
You have to breach the enemy line!

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:23.020
Wh- What are you saying?!

00:22:23.060 --> 00:22:26.030
Are you trying to get
Kou killed in this crossfire?!

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:28.460
<i>Uraki's piloting the Gundam.</i>

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:30.800
That gives him the best
chances of all of us.

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:35.430
Uraki... Our little fight
wasn't just for show, was it?

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:38.740
<i>What's wrong?</i>
<i>Is the little boy scared?</i>

00:22:38.780 --> 00:22:41.040
<i>Then get out now and</i>
<i>I'll take your place!</i>

00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:45.010
Or are you gonna surrender and
give that one to Gato, too?

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:50.820
Ensign Uraki, going in!

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:56.920
What?!

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:16.410
That's pretty damned good for a
wet-behind-the-ears rookie ensign.

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:20.710
<i>All right, time to rescue the</i>
<i>Albion! Follow me, Ensign Uraki!</i>

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:22.180
Yes, sir!

00:23:31.990 --> 00:23:34.390
Captain, please take
the ship higher!

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:37.590
No! We can't just
abandon Bate and Adel!

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:44.470
Dammit! Can't use the
cannons while I'm running!

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:54.780
Not bad, ground pounder!

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:02.220
Forget him!
Concentrate on the ship!

00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:12.620
Enemy base now within
range of our main gun.

00:24:12.670 --> 00:24:14.530
I see it!
The abandoned mine!

00:24:20.380 --> 00:24:22.040
What's that? Fog?

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:23.880
That's an HLV!

00:24:23.910 --> 00:24:26.880
Open the main gun! Lt. Paserov,
you have target control!

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:33.980
Go, Commander Gato!
All units, charge!

00:24:38.090 --> 00:24:39.560
What the?! From the side?!

00:24:42.430 --> 00:24:44.420
We made it in time,
Lieutenant Monsha.

00:24:44.470 --> 00:24:47.560
You see? This is what's
called working in synch.

00:24:47.640 --> 00:24:48.500
<i>Lieutenant!</i>

00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:52.840
I can't lock on with
all this shooting!

00:24:55.180 --> 00:24:57.240
Never mind, just fire!

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:08.880
We've won.
Glory to Operation Stardust.

00:25:14.100 --> 00:25:15.430
They've got boosters!
Shoot them down!

00:25:19.570 --> 00:25:20.330
Heintz!

00:25:23.210 --> 00:25:24.940
Now see our spirit!

00:25:30.410 --> 00:25:31.380
Ensign Uraki!

00:26:47.590 --> 00:26:50.150
Spacenoids...

00:26:50.190 --> 00:26:52.290
So, that's... the enemy.

00:27:18.500 --> 00:27:23.540
<i>Don't come to me just 'cause you're lonely tonight...</i>

00:27:23.540 --> 00:27:28.170
<i>Lonely's only part of your game...</i>

00:27:28.550 --> 00:27:33.970
<i>As long as you live, you must remember one thing...</i>

00:27:33.970 --> 00:27:38.750
<i>Give and take are one and the same...</i>

00:27:38.750 --> 00:27:41.320
<i>So tell me are you ready?</i>

00:27:41.320 --> 00:27:43.990
<i>Really, really ready?</i>

00:27:43.990 --> 00:27:48.500
<i>I don't want your love for one night!</i>

00:27:48.500 --> 00:27:54.290
<i>'Cause I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:27:54.290 --> 00:27:59.150
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near...</i>

00:27:59.490 --> 00:28:04.640
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:28:04.640 --> 00:28:09.810
<i>I need the magic when I touch your hand!</i>

00:28:09.810 --> 00:28:14.970
<i>I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:28:14.970 --> 00:28:20.140
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near!</i>

00:28:20.140 --> 00:28:25.320
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:28:25.320 --> 00:28:32.770
<i>I need the magic when I touch...touch your hand...</i>

00:28:52.250 --> 00:28:54.020
NEXT EPISODE

00:28:55.180 --> 00:28:59.170
Trivial remarks.
Insignificant missed opportunities.

00:28:59.220 --> 00:29:02.590
Ripples that spread
far across the galaxy.

00:29:02.620 --> 00:29:05.220
The iron-willed Delaz Fleet.

00:29:05.260 --> 00:29:08.160
As great words make
the universe tremble...

00:29:08.190 --> 00:29:12.220
...a new and mighty enemy rises
to meet Uraki's Gundam Unit 1.

00:29:13.170 --> 00:29:15.160
A defeated Gundam.

00:29:15.200 --> 00:29:17.190
As Uraki suffers in
his predicament...

00:29:17.240 --> 00:29:19.500
...the waves of
destiny wash over Nina.

00:29:17.780 --> 00:29:22.300
GUNDAM, TO THE
SEA OF STARS
